19. The main contentions raised by defendant in support of his case that :
a.) No transaction has ever taken place between the parties; b.) Case is not filed against the defendant or his proprietorship concern and that plaintiff did not even know the name of defendant prior to filing of the present suit;
c.) No document on record to show business relations between the parties;
d.) Invoices disputed as the same were not signed by any person or CS No. 293/2022 Delhi Alu Company Vs. Food Canteen Rohini Court Page No. 8 of 21 to whom the goods were supplied;
e.) No cause of action at all against the defendant.
20.

In these circumstances, an adverse inference can be drawn against the defendant under secton 114(g) of Indian Evidence Act which reads as under :
(g) that evidence which could be and is not produced would, if produced, be unfavourable to the person who withholds it;
36.

